<title>INDIA: Indian bullion market closed for Hindu festival.</title>
<headline>Indian bullion market closed for Hindu festival.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bombay bullion market was closed on Monday for a Hindu festival. It reopens on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, standard gold closed 20 rupees lower at 4,720 rupees per 10 grammes. Gold biscuits (116.50 grammes each) closed 300 rupees down at 55,200 rupees.</p>
<p>Silver ended five rupees lower at 7,335 rupees per kg. (Conversion $1=35.88 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22 265 9000</p>
</text>
